TASK:{"title":"SWEN3204 Software Architecture – Assignment 2: Short-Answer Questions","overview":"Answer six short questions applying architecture concepts to the CampusEats scenario. The assignment is worth 40 marks, including 4 marks for communication. Submit an individual, single-document response."}
RUBRIC:[{"id":"C1","name":"Q1 Quality attributes","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"Two attributes that clearly matter most are chosen and justified from the scenario. Both scenarios have all six parts and both response measures are measurable."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"Suitable attributes are chosen with some justification. Scenarios are mostly complete but one is missing a part or has a response measure that is not measurable."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Attributes are named with little or no justification, or the scenarios are not in six-part form or are not measurable."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or irrelevant."}]},{"id":"C2","name":"Q2 Architectural style","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"A clear recommendation justified by at least two trade-offs that are specific to the scenario (team size, load profile, known problems). The downside of the recommendation is acknowledged."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"A clear recommendation with two trade-offs, but one is generic or not linked to the scenario, or no downside is acknowledged."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"A recommendation with only one trade-off, or with generic textbook advantages and disadvantages only."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or no recommendation."}]},{"id":"C3","name":"Q3 Availability calculation","weight":null,"max":8,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":7,"max":8,"desc":"Parts (a), (b) and (c) are all correct with working shown, to the requested precision."},{"label":"Proficient","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"The method is correct throughout but there is one arithmetic or rounding slip, or exactly one part is incorrect."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":4,"desc":"The series calculation is attempted but two or more parts are incorrect, or working is not shown."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or no correct element."}]},{"id":"C4","name":"Q4 Resilience pattern","weight":null,"max":5,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":5,"desc":"An appropriate pattern is named, its mechanism is explained correctly, it is applied to the outage, and at least one drawback or tuning consideration is given."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"An appropriate pattern is named and explained correctly, but it is only loosely applied to the outage or no drawback or tuning consideration is given."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"A pattern is named but the explanation is incorrect or very thin."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted or an unsuitable pattern."}]},{"id":"C5","name":"Q5 Consistency and availability","weight":null,"max":6,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":6,"desc":"Both choices are justified, the CAP theorem is used correctly, and a suitable concrete technique is named for each case."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"Both choices are reasonable and techniques are named, but the CAP theorem is explained incorrectly or imprecisely, or one technique is missing."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Choices are stated with little justification, or the CAP theorem is not used."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted."}]},{"id":"C6","name":"Q6 Architecture decision record","weight":null,"max":5,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":5,"max":5,"desc":"Context, Decision and Consequences are all present and specific to the scenario, with at least one positive and one negative consequence."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":4,"desc":"All three sections are present but the consequences are one-sided (no negative consequence) or the context is generic."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"One or more sections are missing or the record does not describe a decision."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Not attempted."}]},{"id":"C7","name":"Communication and format","weight":null,"max":4,"levels":[{"label":"Excellent","min":4,"max":4,"desc":"Every answer is within 150 words, terminology is precise, the required headings are used and sources are cited in IEEE style."},{"label":"Proficient","min":3,"max":3,"desc":"Clear writing, but one answer exceeds the word limit or there are minor citation or formatting problems."},{"label":"Developing","min":1,"max":2,"desc":"Several answers exceed the word limit, or the writing is hard to follow, or sources are not cited."},{"label":"Missing","min":0,"max":0,"desc":"Format requirements ignored."}]}]
MARKING:{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","met":"partial","where":"Question 1"},{"id":"R2","met":"yes","where":"Question 2"},{"id":"R3","met":"partial","where":"Question 3"},{"id":"R4","met":"yes","where":"Question 4"},{"id":"R5","met":"partial","where":"Question 5"},{"id":"R6","met":"partial","where":"Question 6"},{"id":"R7","met":"partial","where":"Question 3; References"}],"technical_issues":[{"where":"Question 1","issue":"The availability response measure, “stay up most of the time,” is not measurable."},{"where":"Question 3","issue":"Part (c) reports payment availability as end-to-end order-placement availability. Including the other components gives approximately 99.80% end-to-end availability and 1.5 hours of monthly downtime."},{"where":"Question 5","issue":"CAP does not permit choosing consistency and availability during a network partition while giving up partition tolerance; consistency-focused behavior sacrifices availability for affected requests during the partition."},{"where":"Question 6","issue":"An offline tablet can prevent or delay notification, but does not necessarily mean the paid order itself is lost; distinguish order persistence from notification delivery."}],"overall":"29/40. Strong scenario-specific architecture recommendation and resilience explanation. Main deductions are for the incorrect end-to-end calculation in Q3(c), the CAP explanation, missing measurable availability target, and Q2 exceeding the word limit.","criteria":[{"id":"C1","level":"Proficient","mark":4.0,"scale":6.0,"points":4.0,"max":6.0,"reasoning":"Performance is justified by the lunch-hour demand and current response time, and its scenario has a measurable response measure. The availability scenario includes the six parts and is relevant, but its measure, “most of the time,” is not measurable.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 1","quote":"The p95 response time is under 1.5 s and no requests are dropped."},{"where":"Question 1","quote":"The system should stay up most of the time."}]},{"id":"C2","level":"Excellent","mark":6.0,"scale":6.0,"points":6.0,"max":6.0,"reasoning":"The modular-monolith recommendation is supported by scenario-specific trade-offs concerning the five-person team, operational overhead, the VM and deployment problems, and the cost of a rewrite. It also acknowledges reduced independent scaling and shared-process risk.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 2","quote":"With five developers, running eight or ten services would mean more time spent on infrastructure than on features."},{"where":"Question 2","quote":"The trade-off I accept is that modules cannot be scaled independently, and a bug in one module can still crash the whole process."}]},{"id":"C3","level":"Proficient","mark":5.0,"scale":8.0,"points":5.0,"max":8.0,"reasoning":"Parts (a) and (b) are correctly calculated and rounded. In (c), the redundant payment-provider availability is calculated correctly, but it is incorrectly reported as end-to-end availability and used directly for system downtime; the other required components are omitted.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 3","quote":"A = 0.9995 × 0.999 × 0.9995 × 0.995 = 0.99301"},{"where":"Question 3","quote":"Downtime = (1 − 0.99301) × 720 = 0.00699 × 720 = 5.0 hours per month."},{"where":"Question 3","quote":"So the new availability of placing an order is 99.9975%"}]},{"id":"C4","level":"Excellent","mark":5.0,"scale":5.0,"points":5.0,"max":5.0,"reasoning":"The circuit breaker mechanism and states are explained correctly, applied to the slow-provider outage, and connected to keeping other application functions responsive. The specified failure threshold and time window provide a tuning consideration.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 4","quote":"When failures exceed a threshold (for example 50% of calls in 10 seconds) the breaker moves to Open"}]},{"id":"C5","level":"Proficient","mark":3.0,"scale":6.0,"points":3.0,"max":6.0,"reasoning":"The choices are reasonable and concrete techniques are named: a cached menu and payment idempotency. However, the CAP explanation is incorrect: during a partition, a system cannot guarantee both consistency and availability; choosing consistency means sacrificing availability for affected requests, not partition tolerance.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 5","quote":"The CAP theorem says a system can only provide two of consistency, availability and partition tolerance"},{"where":"Question 5","quote":"each order request carries an idempotency key"}]},{"id":"C6","level":"Proficient","mark":3.0,"scale":5.0,"points":3.0,"max":5.0,"reasoning":"Context, decision, and consequences are present and specific to outlet notifications. Consequences are positive only; the record does not acknowledge a negative consequence such as eventual delivery, queue/worker operations, or handling duplicates.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 6","quote":"Placing an order no longer waits for the outlet, so the response time improves."}]},{"id":"C7","level":"Proficient","mark":3.0,"scale":4.0,"points":3.0,"max":4.0,"reasoning":"The required headings and order are used, writing is generally clear, and external sources have numbered citations and a reference list. Question 2 exceeds the 150-word limit (approximately 180 words), so the answer does not meet the excellent format descriptor.","evidence":[{"where":"Question 2","quote":"A rewrite would freeze feature work for months without directly fixing either problem."}]}]}
